        "type": "tensor",
        "dtype": "torch.float32",
        "device": "cuda",
        "shape": "same as x"
      },
      "semantics": [
        "Performs BatchNorm2d normalization: y = (x - running_mean) / sqrt(running_var + eps) * weight + bias when not training and running stats are available; otherwise uses batch statistics.",
        "Weight and bias may be None if affine=False; running_mean and running_var may be None if track_running_stats=False.",
        "Normalization is per channel: C dimension; mean and variance are computed over N,H,W if training.",
        "Output dtype float32, same device as input.",
        "Arguments are positional; training flag is a bool, eps and momentum are floats."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "triplet_margin_loss_forward",
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "anchor",
          "kind": "tensor",
          "dtype": "torch.float32",
          "device": "cuda",
          "shape": "[N, *]",
          "layout": "supports strides",
          "nullable": false,
          "optional": false
        },
        {
          "name": "positive",
          "kind": "tensor",
          "dtype": "torch.float32",
          "device": "cuda",
          "shape": "[N, *]",
          "layout": "supports strides",
          "nullable": false,
          "optional": false
        },
        {
          "name": "negative",
          "kind": "tensor",
          "dtype": "torch.float32",
          "device": "cuda",
          "shape": "[N, *]",
          "layout": "supports strides",
          "nullable": false,
          "optional": false
        },
        {
          "name": "p",
          "kind": "float",
          "nullable": false,
          "optional": false
        },
        {
          "name": "margin",
          "kind": "float",
          "nullable": false,
          "optional": false
        }
      ],
      "returns": {
        "type": "tensor",
        "dtype": "torch.float32",
        "device": "cuda",
        "shape": "[]",
        "layout": "contiguous"
      },
      "semantics": [
        "Computes TripletMarginLoss with sum reduction: loss = sum(max(d(anchor, positive) - d(anchor, negative) + margin, 0)), where d is p-norm distance.",
        "p=2 means Euclidean distance squared? Reference: nn.TripletMarginLoss with p=2 computes pairwise distance squared (||a-b||^2) as internal distance, so loss = sum(max(||a-p||^2 - ||a-n||^2 + margin, 0)).",
        "Margin=1.0 as specified.",
        "Reduction is sum over batch; output is a scalar tensor on same device.",
        "Input tensors must have same batch size and feature dimensions; broadcasting follows reference."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "reference_steps": [
